 Yes — the Prometheus path is now built in.

  What changed:

  - FastAPI securely proxies Prometheus queries:
      - GET /api/v1/prometheus/query
      - GET /api/v1/prometheus/query_range
      - GET /api/v1/prometheus/telemetry

  - Dashboard Settings now includes “Prometheus (via Strata-X API)” as a live
    source.

  - Prometheus readings are converted into the same sensor packet format already
    used by the dashboard.

  - Android can use the same backend APIs—without embedding Prometheus
    credentials.

  - Added setup and API documentation: PROMETHEUS_INTEGRATION.md

  To configure it:

  cd /home/umang/Desktop/Strata-x/Dashboard/strata-x/backend
  cp .env.example .env

  Edit .env and set:

  PROMETHEUS_URL=http://YOUR_PROMETHEUS_SERVER:9090
  PROMETHEUS_BEARER_TOKEN=your-token-if-required
  PROMETHEUS_TELEMETRY_QUERY=mine_sensor_reading

  Then start the backend:

  python3 -m pip install -r requirements.txt
  uvicorn main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000

  In the dashboard, go to Settings:

  1. Select Prometheus (via Strata-X API)
  2. Enter http://YOUR_BACKEND_IP:8000
  3. Save Configuration

  Your Prometheus metric needs labels such as:

  mine_sensor_reading{
    node_id="NODE-01",
    sensor_type="methane",
    zone_id="ZONE-P4B",
    unit="% Vol"
  } 0.42

  The Android app should call the FastAPI server, for example:

  GET http://YOUR_BACKEND_IP:8000/api/v1/prometheus/telemetry
  GET
  http://YOUR_BACKEND_IP:8000/api/v1/prometheus/query?query=mine_sensor_reading

  TypeScript, production build, and backend Python syntax validation all pass.


